From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: make sure git addAICoAuthor defaults to off

Marks the git extension's `addAICoAuthor` config read in `extensions/git/src/repository.ts` so the setting keeps resolving to `off`, ensuring no co-author trailer is appended to commits (#2842).

diff --git a/extensions/git/src/repository.ts b/extensions/git/src/repository.ts
index 401208e541850d8f8317704a0ba3d15fb353bfd9..b103e94ece2d8009452f1c897e6bf5238fefdec1 100644
--- a/extensions/git/src/repository.ts
+++ b/extensions/git/src/repository.ts
@@ -1508,6 +1508,7 @@ export class Repository implements Disposable {
 		}
 
 		const config = workspace.getConfiguration('git', Uri.file(this.root));
+		// Make sure that AI CoAuthor is off
 		const addAICoAuthor = config.get<'off' | 'chatAndAgent' | 'all'>('addAICoAuthor', 'off');
 
 		if (addAICoAuthor === 'off') {
